00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.660
<b>Top News</b>

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.660
<b>Close-up Coverage of the Child
 Actress Currently Making Waves!!</b>

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:00.140
Sueharu-oniichan! What's your favorite food?

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.270
Huh? Well, uh...

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.340
Maru-chan, you're up.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.530
Sorry, I gotta go.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:09.010
Momo-chan...

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.830
I can tell you what Haru-kun's 
favorite foods are.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.330
Mother!

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:19.400
Haru-kun likes Japanese-style meat and potato 
stew, fried chicken, and things like that.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.540
He especially loves miso soup.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:25.220
If he doesn't have some for breakfast,
 he gets really mad.

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:29.550
U-Um...

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:33.580
Could you... teach me how to make it?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.290
Of course.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.660
Why don't we make some together?

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.350
<i>When the subject of the 
documentary came up,</i>

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:49.470
<i>I started to think, 
and I came to a conclusion.</i>

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:55.780
<i>When we each have our turns to dig deeper 
into our pasts with Sueharu-oniichan,</i>

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.270
<i>the one who'll benefit 
the most from it is me.</i>

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:03.950
<i>The biggest event in Sueharu-oniichan's 
past was what happened to his mother.</i>

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:09.450
<i>When he has to face that, he'll feel sad,
 whether he wants to or not.</i>

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.360
<b>Momo</b>

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.360
<b>Sueharu-oniichan...</b>

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.750
<i>By being with him when that happens,</i>

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:15.740
<b>Move closer to him</b>

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:15.740
<b>Ask someone for advice</b>

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:15.800
<i>he'll realize that I can share both 
the good times and the bad ones with him,</i>

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.470
<i>and he'll like me more!</i>

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.910
<i>By holding him gently, I can 
emphasize how accepting I am!</i>

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.740
<i>Then I'll break free of the 
"little sister" image, and...</i>

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.620
<i>Momo is the winner!</i>

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:35.110
This is where I wanted to bring you.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.600
Are you angry?

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.550
Nah.

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:46.070
I knew I'd have to come 
here sooner or later.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.280
Sueharu-oniichan...

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.000
I know it's painful,

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:00.120
but could you tell me about 
how your mother passed away?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.590
Okay.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:08.780
Mom was lying on the ground right here.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:14.300
In <i>Child King</i>, the protagonist's 
mother dies in the first episode.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:17.520
It was supposed to be just for that scene.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:23.870
The police investigated and found out that 
the car never even made contact with her.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.970
Mom had experience with stunt roles,

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.450
but she tried so hard to make her own 
stunt realistic that she hit her head.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:33.170
She hit it in just the wrong spot.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.480
It really was a freak accident.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:43.200
When it was announced that Mom had died 
and filming of <i>Child King</i> would cease,

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.670
I opposed it more than anyone else.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.240
Mom gave her life for the role 
she'd dreamed of playing,

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.870
and I couldn't bear seeing it go to waste.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.150
That's why I poured all of my energy 
into my role in <i>Child King</i>.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:02.350
Because it was my first and last 
time acting alongside my mom.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.310
<b>HOT TOPIC RANKING</b>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.310
<b>20 WEEKS IN A ROW</b>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.310
<b>NUMBER</b>

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:05.310
But when filming stopped,

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.170
I was like a kite whose 
string had been cut.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.970
Every time I thought about 
Mom, I couldn't act...

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.660
So I left show business.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.470
That's the true story of my retirement.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.280
Thank you for sharing such 
a painful confession.

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:27.220
Are you all right?

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.540
Huh? Yeah, I'm not sure what it is.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.890
I feel like I'm really sad,

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.320
but no tears are coming.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:39.790
How is "feeling like you're sad" 
different from "feeling sad"?

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:43.360
Maybe I'm just confused... 
I'm not really sure.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.810
I'm not even sure what "sad" means.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:52.570
Is that how you felt when 
filming <i>Child King</i>, too?

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:54.980
I'm not sure.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:59.120
Now that I look back on it, 
something did feel off.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:01.980
But I never would have thought 
all that had happened.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:06.950
Even if I was still in elementary school,
 my staff could have told me!

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:08.500
Then I...

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:13.700
You're amazing, Onii-chan! You're a hero!

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:16.470
There's no way you can stop acting!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.660
<i>No! This isn't the time for me to complain!</i>

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.020
<i>I won't let my feelings 
get the better of me.</i>

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.740
<i>I won't regret anything else.</i>

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:29.620
<i>I have to keep this up according to plan!</i>

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:35.580
What's wrong?

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:42.790
I'm... sorry.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.230
Momo?

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:50.990
I always... felt like I needed 
to apologize to you.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:56.730
So many things seemed wrong, 
and I was in a position to notice,

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.920
but I didn't notice a thing.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:05.130
And on top of that, I said 
something so awful..

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:08.510
That doesn't bother me, really.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:12.090
You say that because you're 
such a nice person,

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:16.740
but I can't stand how incompetent I am!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.790
All I've ever thought about is myself.

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:26.340
Both back then and now, I just 
say whatever I want to say.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:29.350
And I can't forgive myself for it!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.990
I see you're still a perfectionist, Momo.

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:41.350
I know you won't just do what 
I tell you that easily,

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.100
but don't worry about it.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.270
I...

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:49.710
I loved your mother, Sueharu-oniichan.

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:54.180
She was so kind and pretty.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:58.330
She was the ideal mother in my mind.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:05.520
So... when I found out she died...

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.870
I was... so sad.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.550
Haru-kun...

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:16.990
Mom...

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.620
Mom!

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:20.820
Mom...

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:26.930
Huh?

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.340
That's weird... Why now?

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:36.030
Sorry.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:38.880
For some reason, I suddenly feel...

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.180
really sad...

00:21:57.760 --> 00:22:00.160
It's okay, Onii-chan.

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:04.060
That's only natural.
